  message: "Completed both parts.\n\nPART 1 — dash/underscore dupes harmonized (7 renames, 21 item-tag rewrites):\n- analysis-quality (4) → analysis_quality (total 287, +4)\n- ci-infrastructure (1) → ci_infrastructure (total 38, +1)\n- self-analysis (1) → self_analysis (total 47, +1) [not in original item body — surfaced by 2026-05-23 tags --count audit]\n- phase-2 (12) → phase_2 (was 0/inactive; now 12 active)\n- phase-2b (1) → phase_2b (NEW snake form) [not in original item body — surfaced by audit; phase-2b is a legit Rust Phase 2b sub-phase tag on WI-bifog]\n- entrypoints (1) → entrypoint (total 5)\n- entrypoint_detection (1) → entrypoint (consolidated; was on INV-tajap)\n\nPART 2 — 7 missing concept tags added via tracker tags describe (each carries a one-line definition; usage starts at 0/inactive, ready to be adopted by future items):\nranking, dampener, centrality, wheel, sha256, citation, span_construct.\n\nCanonical direction confirmed by _TAG_NAME_RE = ^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$ (dashes are illegal under current validation). All old dash forms now show inactive in tracker tags --count.\n\nFollow-up worth filing separately (not in this item's scope): many other tags still violate _TAG_NAME_RE (adr-0017, io-boundary, phase-0/-1/-3, stable-id, external-bakeoff, bakeoff-revalidation, formal-methods, supply-chain, taint-flow, test-coverage, tracker-hygiene, etc., 20+ entries). These were grandfathered before the regex tightened. A separate sweep could harmonize them, but the WI-fanus body did not request it."  # 8b8e
